    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0458" n="436" xml:id="pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/1–2252: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Embassy in Greece and to the United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Austin</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d315-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1952-01-22T10:52:00-05:00">January 22,
                            1952—10: 52 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Grk Rep informed Dept of approach by Ital UN Del in which latter is said to have stated Ital
                    belief US attitude toward Sov “package” admission plan had changed. According
                    Grk Rep Ital stated US, instead of voting against Sov proposal, wld abstain and
                    added this wld make Grk vote most important in attainment Ital ambition UN membership. Grks replied that while desirous
                    aiding Itals if possible, they wld for obvious reasons have be very careful
                    about any res which wld admit Alb and Bulg to UN
                    membership. Grk Rep then asked for info re US position this subj.</p>
                <p>Grk Rep was informed that USDel wld make it
                    clear that we were against this Res. If vote for Res failed show seven
                    affirmative, US wld vote against. If affirmative vote showed seven in favor, US
                    wld abstain in view its policy of not exercising veto on membership
                    question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d315-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d315-f1-content">
